      en: { q: "Which statements about the circular flow of the economy are correct? Select all that apply.", o: ["Households provide businesses with labour and receive income in return.", "Banks accept savings and grant loans to businesses and households.", "The simple circular flow already includes banks and the state.", "The state collects taxes and pays, for example, subsidies to businesses.", "Households pay banks interest for keeping their savings."], e: "The simple circular flow only shows businesses ↔ households; banks are added in the extended model and the state only in the complete one. Households RECEIVE interest on savings – interest is paid by whoever takes out a loan." },
