      en: { q: "A taxi operator from Graz buys a new estate car to transport passengers. His neighbour buys exactly the same model for family trips. How should the two cars be classified?", o: ["Both are consumer goods because it is the same model", "Both are capital goods because cars are durable", "Taxi: capital good – neighbour's car: consumer good", "Taxi: consumer good – neighbour's car: capital good"], e: "The operator uses the car to produce his service (rides) – capital good. The neighbour uses it privately – consumer good. The fact that it is the same model or lasts long is irrelevant." },
